          "content": "I need you to write a JSON Patch to update the existing state with the new information.\n\nCurrent State:\n{\n  \"time\": \"14:15\",\n  \"location\": \"Kitchen\",\n  \"characters\": {\n    \"Tom\": {\n      \"location\": \"Kitchen\",\n      \"clothing\": {\n        \"0\": \"blue shirt\",\n        \"1\": \"jeans\"\n      },\n      \"mood\": \"annoyed\"\n    },\n    \"Susie\": {\n      \"location\": \"Bedroom\",\n      \"clothing\": {\n        \"0\": \"red dress\"\n      },\n      \"mood\": \"happy\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"doorLocked\": true,\n  \"playerHasKey\": false\n}\n\nNew Information:\nExactly five minutes pass.\n\nAdd a patch operation only when the value in the updated state should be different from the current state.\n\nFor this version, arrays in Current State are shown as objects with their zero-based indexes as keys. They're still arrays in the actual state, so use those numbers as array indexes in JSON Patch paths.\n\nPlease return only the JSON Patch array."
